ol_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.15581342343675794,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.00722,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":4.8,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Reddit, Inc. operates a digital community in the United States and internationally. The company's platform enables user to engage in conversations, explore passions, research new hobbies, exchange goods and services, create new communities and experiences, share laughs, and find belonging. It also organizes communities based on specific interests that enable users to engage in conversations by sharing experiences, submitting links, uploading images and videos, and replying to one another. Reddit, Inc. was founded in 2005 and is headquartered in San Francisco, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Steven Ladd Huffman | Co-Founder, CEO, President & Director | Age 41 | Compensation: $3.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $862K ranks in the above the sector median among Communication Services peers. Each employee generates $268K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $134K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Reddit, Inc. is a large-cap communication services business with a $18.1B market cap on $2.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +69% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +63.2pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -37% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $684M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 31 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.30\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 16% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 126% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.2646148498473408},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Communication Services peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (14.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $33.4M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Advertising-cycle exposure and content/regulatory risk \u2014 a single platform policy shift or ad-spend contraction cascades through the P&L quickly.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cord-cutting acceleration and audience fragmentation \u2014 legacy distribution bundles unravel faster than subscription revenue can replace them.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI-generated content commoditisation \u2014 as creation costs collapse toward zero, content libraries lose pricing power and differentiation narrows.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 11% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Growing faster than most Communication Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Among the least levered in Communication Services \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Why Reddit (RDDT) Is Getting Attention Today","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/media/nyse-rddt/reddit/news/why-reddit-rddt-is-getting-attention-today","date":"2026-11-26","timestamp":1795709465.651,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.878,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"How Did Reddit (NYSE:RDDT) Lift Its Quarterly Revenue So Sharply?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/communication/how-did-reddit-nyserddt-lift-its-quarterly-revenue-so-sharply","date":"2026-11-26","timestamp":1795694040.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.778,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Technical Reactions to RDDT Trends in Macro Strategies","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/15/Technical_Reactions_to_RDDT_Trends_in_Macro_Strategies_112526113802_